{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":496711,"name":"Gomer","username":"Gomer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T08:36:14.825Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok bot cannot add a line to a simple diagram correctly\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI tried to provide my image files, but new users are limited.  I can share if anyone asks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd a line to a small graphic that is parallel and emanates from the same connecting line as two other lines.   Fail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/f/3f299bc06fb85bb4641c1462836cef3cfe634a5e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/90Le1E9tzSDyIAYrFfvLaSTmNj0.png?dl=1\" title=\"bug-001.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/f/3f299bc06fb85bb4641c1462836cef3cfe634a5e.png\" alt=\"bug-001.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"90Le1E9tzSDyIAYrFfvLaSTmNj0\" width=\"690\" height=\"246\" data-dominant-color=\"ECEBF0\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebug-001.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e877×313 12.4 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot app: 0.47.0 (amd64, package grok-bot on your machine)\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Linux (Ubuntu 24.04-class) — host gomer-X870-GAMING-X-WIFI7\u003cbr\u003e\nBot computer Chrome: 151.0.7922.169\u003cbr\u003e\nDate: 2026-09-21\u003cbr\u003e\nIf the form wants a long “Cursor Version” string, paste something like: Grok Bot 0.47.0 amd64 / Linux / box Chrome 151.0.7922.169\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496711-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496711-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T18:11:20.793Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":30.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172484,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable","display_username":"Gomer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138988,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable/172484/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":496720,"name":"Gomer","username":"Gomer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T08:39:44.095Z","cooked":"\u003cdiv class=\"d-image-grid\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/b/3bc180b081b719bbf372196d6f791a24647e51d4.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/8wCKoIicP4DU1QOs8mBS5WdZt1W.png?dl=1\" title=\"bot_002\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/b/3bc180b081b719bbf372196d6f791a24647e51d4_2_690x497.png\" alt=\"bot_002\" data-base62-sha1=\"8wCKoIicP4DU1QOs8mBS5WdZt1W\" width=\"690\" height=\"497\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/b/3bc180b081b719bbf372196d6f791a24647e51d4_2_690x497.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/b/3bc180b081b719bbf372196d6f791a24647e51d4_2_1035x745.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/b/3bc180b081b719bbf372196d6f791a24647e51d4_2_1380x994.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F7F5F4\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebot_002\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1903×1373 157 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/e/2/e285e8173dacb8f5b9da416b4cb26a817e268457.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/wjUNIuVyI9nZZt6cXQ3FpI8rmp9.png?dl=1\" title=\"bug-002\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/e/2/e285e8173dacb8f5b9da416b4cb26a817e268457.png\" alt=\"bug-002\" data-base62-sha1=\"wjUNIuVyI9nZZt6cXQ3FpI8rmp9\" width=\"566\" height=\"233\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebug-002\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e566×233 5.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/c/dc5e4c851c287b0a3990feac8dc73858a328874d.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/vrt4PJe9ysSjltTzrpU1epDAELr.png?dl=1\" title=\"bug-003\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/c/dc5e4c851c287b0a3990feac8dc73858a328874d.png\" alt=\"bug-003\" data-base62-sha1=\"vrt4PJe9ysSjltTzrpU1epDAELr\" width=\"671\" height=\"233\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebug-003\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e671×233 7.81 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere is the starting source, the first try is in the bug report, these are subsequent tries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe had many discussions on how to connect the middle line (in blue above) to the black feeder line on the left.   Hours actually.   I was trying to discern how the bot was trying to figure out how to make the new lines endpoint (on the left) intersect the black feeder line that the two other lines are touching.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T08:39:44.095Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172484,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable","display_username":"Gomer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138988,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable/172484/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":496780,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T09:54:55.944Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report and for adding the original plan and the follow-up attempts. It makes it immediately clear what happened. Sorry it took so long to get there.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA bit of context. When the bot edits an already finished image, it doesn’t have a visual drawing tool where it can see the canvas. It looks at the image, estimates the pixel positions of the existing lines and the feeder curve, then writes a small script that draws a new line using those coordinates. Estimating exact positions from a raster image is exactly where the model can be off, so each attempt ends up slightly misaligned or doesn’t quite reach the curve. This is a limitation of how accurately the model reads geometry from a raster, not something broken in the app, so this kind of edit probably won’t be stable today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat usually works noticeably better:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf the plan exists in a vector or editable format (SVG, \u003ca href=\"http://draw.io\"\u003edraw.io\u003c/a\u003e, CAD/DXF export, or the file from the app it was drawn in), give the bot that instead of a PNG. Then it can add the third siding with exact geometry (same angle as the neighboring ones, endpoint exactly on the feeder curve) and export a new PNG.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you only have a PNG, split the task into two steps. First: “Find the two black lines inside the blue Goods Handling block and the feeder curve on the left that they connect to. Give the exact pixel coordinates of the endpoints of each line and the points where they intersect the curve.” Check those numbers against the image. Then ask it to draw a new line using those coordinates (“same length and angle, start on the curve halfway between the two connection points”).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOr ask it to redraw the entire plan as an SVG, then iterate on the SVG. Vector output is much more predictable than pixel edits, and each follow-up edit becomes precise.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you try one of these options and the line still doesn’t land correctly, share the exact wording of your request and I’ll take another look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T09:54:55.944Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172484,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://draw.io","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Flowchart Maker \u0026 Online Diagram Software","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable/172484/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":496838,"name":"Gomer","username":"Gomer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:33:53.242Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eOk thanks for the quick response.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou may want to check the session since I had a long conversation with the bot about how to best tackle this and vector vs raster never came up as a solution.   I use GIMP, so SVG is as good as it can do.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt’s pretty limited so maybe this isn’t the best way to go about this activity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt did fine on the layout stack up of the build out of the table, the seam support, ply support and top layer modules, but the track planning and layout seems pretty difficult unless I do all that in another SW tool.   Is that where I am at on this?   I’m OK with it, just looking for guidance.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T10:33:53.242Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172484,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable","display_username":"Gomer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138988,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable/172484/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":496884,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T11:07:31.749Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYes, you got it mostly right. For precise geometry like track planning, aligning lines, and snapping to a feeder curve, raster editing isn’t the best approach today. Layout diagrams like a table stackup or seam and ply support work fine because they don’t require sub pixel accuracy. But a line that needs to run at the exact same angle and end exactly on a curve is exactly where estimating coordinates from an image falls apart.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGIMP isn’t an ideal source here since it’s mainly raster based. A vector tool is a better fit for this kind of work.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInkscape is free, available on Ubuntu, and works with SVG natively. You can sketch the plan there or import a PNG as a background and trace it, then give the bot an SVG. That way it edits exact coordinates instead of guessing from pixels.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://draw.io\"\u003edraw.io\u003c/a\u003e is great for schematic layouts like a track plan, and objects stay editable.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter that, iterating with the bot on SVG becomes predictable. Requests like “extend this line until it intersects the curve” or “match the angle of the neighboring one” work accurately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbout the bot not suggesting a vector approach earlier in the conversation, that’s fair feedback. I’ll pass it along. Ideally it should suggest this before you spend hours on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you try Inkscape with SVG and something still doesn’t line up, share the exact wording of your request and I’ll take another look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T11:07:31.749Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172484,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://draw.io","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Flowchart Maker \u0026 Online Diagram Software","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":138988,"username":"Gomer","name":"Gomer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/3ec8ea/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-simple-image-track-geometry-edit-unreliable/172484/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":497039,"name":"Gomer","username":"